---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About — Your Site" description="A short introduction to the team and what they do.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-3">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-5xl">Hello, friend.</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      This is the about page. Replace this copy with a short story about the business: who runs it, what it does, who it serves. A few paragraphs is plenty.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      Keep it human. Say what you care about and why. Avoid marketing fluff. If someone new lands on this page, they should finish it knowing whether they want to work with you.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">What we do</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      One paragraph on the service, product, or mission. Short. Specific. No jargon.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground">Get in touch</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      The <a href="/contact" class="text-primary hover:underline">contact page</a> has the details.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
